    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92020" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥά</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, enclit. Particle, 
			Ep.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρα</span> (q.v.), freq. in
		Hom.and <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
		</span></i>; less freq. in Trag. (lyr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ ῥα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					633
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				172
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤ ῥα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				177
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				18.33
			</span></i>.—This and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κα</span> are the
			only monosyll. Particles not ending in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ε</span>
			which allow elision.</div>
